{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For the foundations</b> — nets, as in: 'and their nets shall be crushed.' Some say: foundations, as in 'exposing the foundations,' and the witness shall destroy — this is an allusion to counsels, which are like foundations." "<b>And the meaning of 'what has the righteous done'</b> — for this is the deed of Elohim; do not rage against the righteous. Therefore, after him: 'YHWH — in His holy palace,' which is the heavens." "<b>His eyes behold</b> — corresponding to 'to shoot in the dark.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The three-word phrase 'וחשופי שת והעד יהרסון' appears to be a fragmentary quotation, possibly from a piyyut; translated hyper-literally without resolving its context."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:01.215197187Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}